// Demo of the templating-loop feature: one request block below expands into N
// independent, fully-reported requests - one per item in the 'Partners'
// collection set in the -init.csx script. NOTE: avoid writing literal loop-tag
// syntax inside a comment like this one - the scanner runs on raw file text
// before comments are stripped, so a comment merely describing the tags would
// itself be mistaken for a malformed tag.
//
// Notice that '{{ApiBaseUrl}}' (TeaPie's own variable, resolved AFTER expansion)
// survives untouched, while '{{ partner.Name }}' and '{{ forloop.index }}'
// (Liquid loop-scope expressions, resolved DURING expansion) become real
// values for each iteration.
{% for partner in Partners %}
### Create partner {{ forloop.index }}: {{ partner.Name }}
# @name CreatePartner{{ forloop.index }}
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [201]
POST {{ApiBaseUrl}}/posts
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "{{ partner.Name }}", "body": "Registration ID {{ partner.RegistrationId }}", "userId": {{ forloop.index }} }

{% endfor %}
